## Port of pumpkin/src/plugin/loader/wasm/wasm_host/wit/v0_1/permission.rs: the `permission` interface has only
## types and no functions (`impl Host for PluginHostState {}`), so there is nothing to install; a plugin that imports
## it gets an empty interface from the host.
## Port of pumpkin/src/plugin/loader/wasm/wasm_host/wit/v0_1/java_dialogs.rs: likewise `java-dialogs` has no host
## functions upstream (`impl Host for PluginHostState {}`); nothing to install.
## Port of pumpkin/src/plugin/loader/wasm/wasm_host/wit/mod.rs: only `pub mod v0_1;`; the one API version here is
## v0.1, registered by pluginhost.aowl's installInterfaces.
## Port of pumpkin/src/plugin/loader/wasm/wasm_host/wit/v0_1/logging.rs: `log` is pluginhost.aowl's `logging#log`
## (every level maps to the host log line writer).
## `log-tracing` is pluginhost.aowl's `logging#log-tracing`, decoded by logtracing.aowl.
const WitEmptyInterfaces* = ["pumpkin:plugin/permission", "pumpkin:plugin/java-dialogs"]
